Interactive USD render regions set by the resolution and dataWindowNDC render settings

Two spheres are rendered by the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, then with the
resolution and dataWindowNDC render settings that Houdini sends for a cropped render, the host buffer being the size of
the region: the left half (cropped in x only), the top half (cropped in y only) and the bottom right quarter. The
settings are then cleared. Covers the fix of the regions cropped on a single axis (#2564). See
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last render is compared against
the reference image.

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
